ocs-type"><span class="stldocs-type-preview" data-stldocs-type-preview="union"><span class="stldocs-type-preview-content"><span class="stldocs-type"><span class="stldocs-literal-string">&quot;auto&quot;</span></span><span class="stldocs-text-operator"> <!-- -->or<!-- --> </span><span class="stldocs-type"><span class="stldocs-literal-string">&quot;low&quot;</span></span><span class="stldocs-text-operator"> <!-- -->or<!-- --> </span><span class="stldocs-type"><span class="stldocs-literal-string">&quot;high&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></div><div class="stldocs-property-description"><div class="stldocs-markdown stldocs-content stl-ui-prose"><p>The detail level of the file to be sent to the model. Use <code>auto</code> to let the system select the detail level; for GPT-5.6 and later models, <code>auto</code> uses high-quality rendering, which may increase input token usage. Use <code>low</code> for lower-cost rendering, or <code>high</code> to render the file at higher quality. Defaults to <code>auto</code>.</p>
